.TH POD\-RELEASE 1 "" "pod\-release" "pod\-release manual"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
pod\-release \- Verify a release of a product of PodUtils in a directory: the
signature of SHA256SUMS, each file and the release index
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpod\-release COMMAND [OPTIONS]\fR
.PP
\fBStart here:\fR
.TP
\fBpod\-release verify \-\-repo OWNER/REPO \-\-tag TAG DIR\fR
Verify a release in a directory.
.TP
\fBpod\-release sums DIR\fR
Check a dry run, before the signature.
.TP
\fBpod\-release man\fR
Read the manual.
.PP
\fBVerify a release:\fR
.TP
\fBverify\fR
Verify the signature of SHA256SUMS, then each file, then the release index
.TP
\fBsums\fR
Check each file and the release index against SHA256SUMS, with no signature:
the check of a dry run
.PP
\fBRead a release index:\fR
.TP
\fBindex\fR
Read a release index, and write one line for each file: its name, its target,
its size and its SHA\-256
.PP
\fBRead the manual:\fR
.TP
\fBman\fR
The manual: each command, exit code and variable. A pager shows it on a
terminal
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help.
.SH DESCRIPTION
pod\-release verifies a release of a product of PodUtils in a directory. It
reads files only and uses no network. Download the files with your own tool
first.
.PP
pod\-release verify makes three checks in this order. First, the Sigstore
bundle SHA256SUMS.sigstore.json of SHA256SUMS, against the signer that you
name.
.PP
Then the SHA\-256 of each file against SHA256SUMS. Then release\-index.json
against SHA256SUMS, its schema and the signer.
.PP
The first failure stops the checks. pod\-release writes one line on the error
output that names the failure, and exits with the code of its class.
.PP
With no FILE, pod\-release checks each file of SHA256SUMS that the directory
holds, and names the missing files. With \-\-all, a missing file is a failure.
.PP
pod\-release sums makes the same checks with no signature. A dry run of a
release workflow uses it before the workflow signs SHA256SUMS.
.PP
pod\-release index writes the files of a release index, one line for each
file. Verify the release before you use its index.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "pod\-release verify"
Verify the signature of SHA256SUMS, then each file, then the release index.
.PP
Usage: \fBpod\-release verify [OPTIONS] DIR [FILE]...\fR
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIDIR\fR
The directory that holds SHA256SUMS and the files.
.TP
\fI[FILE]...\fR
Check only these files of the directory, and the index when the directory
holds it. Each must be in SHA256SUMS.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fIOWNER/REPO\fR
The repository of the release on GitHub, as OWNER/REPO. The signer is its
release workflow at the tag.
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fITAG\fR
The tag of the release, as v0.77.0.
.TP
\fB\-\-workflow\fR \fIFILE\fR
The file name of the release workflow in .github/workflows. Default:
release.yml.
.TP
\fB\-\-identity\fR \fIURI\fR
The URI that the certificate of the signer must name. Use it in place of
\-\-repo and \-\-tag.
.TP
\fB\-\-issuer\fR \fIURL\fR
The issuer of the OIDC token of the signer. Default:
https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Each file of SHA256SUMS must be in the directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give one of \-\-repo, \-\-identity.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-identity, \-\-workflow.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-issuer, \-\-repo.
.PP
Give only one of \-\-all, FILE.
.PP
\-\-repo needs \-\-tag.
.PP
\-\-tag needs \-\-repo.
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Verify the release v0.77.0 of podcrates in the directory dist.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release verify \-\-repo PodUtils/podcrates \-\-tag v0.77.0 dist
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify each file of the release. A missing file is a failure.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release verify \-\-repo PodUtils/podcrates \-\-tag v0.77.0 \-\-all dist
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify one file and the index, as an installer does.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release verify \-\-repo PodUtils/podcrates \-\-tag v0.77.0 dist podlab\-x86_64\-unknown\-linux\-musl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify a release by the full identity of its signer.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release verify \-\-identity https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/tags/v1.0.0 dist
.fi
.RE
.SS "pod\-release sums"
Check each file and the release index against SHA256SUMS, with no signature:
the check of a dry run.
.PP
Usage: \fBpod\-release sums [OPTIONS] DIR [FILE]...\fR
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIDIR\fR
The directory that holds SHA256SUMS and the files.
.TP
\fI[FILE]...\fR
Check only these files of the directory, and the index when the directory
holds it. Each must be in SHA256SUMS.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Each file of SHA256SUMS must be in the directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give only one of \-\-all, FILE.
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Check each file and the index of a dry run, before the signature.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release sums \-\-all dist
.fi
.RE
.SS "pod\-release index"
Read a release index, and write one line for each file: its name, its target,
its size and its SHA\-256.
.PP
Usage: \fBpod\-release index [OPTIONS] FILE\fR
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIFILE\fR
The release index, release\-index.json.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fITRIPLE\fR
Write only the files of this target triple. A target with no file gives exit
66.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Write the files of one target from the index.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release index \-\-target x86_64\-unknown\-linux\-musl dist/release\-index.json
.fi
.RE
.SS "pod\-release man"
The manual: each command, exit code and variable. A pager shows it on a
terminal.
.PP
Usage: \fBpod\-release man [OPTIONS] [SECTION]...\fR
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fI[SECTION]...\fR
One section: a command, a topic, a table of facts.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Write the text with no pager, also on a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-roff\fR
Write the manual as a man(7) page.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Write the manual as one JSON object.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give only one of \-\-json, \-\-roff.
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Write the section of pod\-release verify, with no pager.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release man \-\-no\-pager verify
.fi
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
\fBThe pager:\fR
.TP
\fBPAGER\fR
The pager of the manual on a terminal. An empty value or cat writes the text
with no pager. Used by: man.
.TP
\fBTERM\fR
With no PAGER, less is used only when TERM names a terminal that is not dumb.
Used by: man.
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
The directories where the probe looks for less. Used by: man.
.TP
\fBLINES\fR
The lines of a screen of the built\-in pager, when the terminal size is not
known. Used by: man.
.TP
\fBLESS\fR
The options of less. When it is not set, the pager sets FRX. Used by: man.
pod\-release reads it and sets it.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR (ok)
Each check holds.
.TP
\fB64\fR (usage)
A usage error of the command line.
.TP
\fB66\fR (notfound)
A file is not there: SHA256SUMS, its bundle, a file that you name, or a file
of SHA256SUMS with \-\-all.
.TP
\fB69\fR (unavailable)
A file is there, and pod\-release cannot read it.
.TP
\fB77\fR (refused)
A check failed: the signature, the signer, the SHA\-256 of a file, or the
release index.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Verify the release v0.77.0 of podcrates in the directory dist.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release verify \-\-repo PodUtils/podcrates \-\-tag v0.77.0 dist
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify each file of the release. A missing file is a failure.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release verify \-\-repo PodUtils/podcrates \-\-tag v0.77.0 \-\-all dist
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify one file and the index, as an installer does.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release verify \-\-repo PodUtils/podcrates \-\-tag v0.77.0 dist podlab\-x86_64\-unknown\-linux\-musl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify a release by the full identity of its signer.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release verify \-\-identity https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/tags/v1.0.0 dist
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check each file and the index of a dry run, before the signature.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release sums \-\-all dist
.fi
.RE
.PP
Write the files of one target from the index.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release index \-\-target x86_64\-unknown\-linux\-musl dist/release\-index.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Write the section of pod\-release verify, with no pager.
.RS 4
.nf
$ pod\-release man \-\-no\-pager verify
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
cosign verify\-blob: the same check of the bundle, with no check of the files and the index.
.PP
https://github.com/PodUtils/podcrates
